.TH VFX 1 "" "vfx 2.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vfx \- extract still images from video files using ffmpeg
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vfx
[\fB\-R\fR]
[\fB\-W\fR \fImask\fR]
[\fB\-S\fR | \fB\-I\fR | \fB\-\-verbose\fR]
[\fB\-N\fR \fIx\fR | \fB\-T\fR \fIx\fR]
[\fB\-X\fR \fIx\fR]
[\fB\-Y\fR \fIx\fR]
[\fB\-F\fR \fIfmt\fR]
[\fB\-Q\fR \fIx\fR]
[\fB\-M\fR]
[\fB\-P\fR]
[\fB\-D\fR]
[\fB\-O\fR [\fIxx\fR]]
[\fB\-L\fR]
[\fB\-V\fR]
[\fB\-H\fR]
[\fIsource\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vfx
extracts still images from video files.
It can save a number of evenly spaced frames, one frame every
.I x
seconds, or every frame.
.PP
.I source
is a video file or a directory; the default is the current directory.
In a directory, files with a common video extension
(mp4, mov, mkv, avi, webm, mpg, wmv, flv, ts, 3gp and others, in any case)
are processed.
A file named explicitly is processed whatever its extension.
.PP
Images are written to a new folder
.IR name _frames
next to each video, or, with
.BR \-D ,
next to the video itself.
Existing files are never overwritten: a later run creates
.IR name _frames_1 ,
and so on.
.PP
By default one progress line is shown per video, for example:
.PP
.RS
clip.mp4: generated 5 of 16 frames (2 of 7 videos)
.RE
.PP
.B ffmpeg
and
.B ffprobe
must be installed and on the
.BR PATH .
.SH OPTIONS
Single-letter switches are case-insensitive:
.B \-n
is the same as
.BR \-N .
Long options are lowercase only.
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-recursive
Process the directory and all its subdirectories.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-silent
Silent mode: no text output, except
.B \-P
prompts.
.TP
.BR \-I ", " \-\-info
Info mode (the default): one progress line per video, with no output from
ffmpeg.
Cannot be combined with
.BR \-S .
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Show ffmpeg's own output.
Cannot be combined with
.B \-S
or
.BR \-I .
.TP
.BR \-N ", " \-\-count " \fIx\fR"
Extract
.I x
evenly spaced frames per video (default 16).
0 extracts all frames.
Each frame is taken from the middle of its slice of the video.
Cannot be combined with
.BR \-T .
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-interval " \fIx\fR"
Extract one frame every
.I x
seconds; decimals are allowed (for example 0.5).
0 extracts all frames.
.TP
.BR \-W ", " \-\-match " \fImask\fR"
Only process videos whose file name matches the wildcard
.I mask
(\fB*\fR and \fB?\fR, case-insensitive), for example
.BR "\-R \-W '*spain*'" .
Quote the mask so the shell does not expand it.
It applies to folder scans, not to a file named as
.IR source .
Images go where they would without
.BR \-W ;
.B \-D
and
.B \-O
work as usual.
.TP
.BR \-X ", " \-\-width " \fIx\fR"
Image width in pixels.
Without
.B \-Y
the height keeps the aspect ratio.
.TP
.BR \-Y ", " \-\-height " \fIx\fR"
Image height in pixels.
Without
.B \-X
the width keeps the aspect ratio.
.TP
.BR \-F ", " \-\-format " \fIfmt\fR"
Image format:
.BR jpg " (default), " png " or " webp .
.TP
.BR \-Q ", " \-\-quality " \fIx\fR"
Image quality from 1 to 100, higher is better.
Applies to jpg and webp only.
Default: best quality for jpg, 90 for webp.
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-\-timestamps
Name images by their timestamp in the video
(\fIname\fR_HH\-MM\-SS.mmm.jpg) instead of a counter (\fIname\fR_001.jpg).
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-prompt
Ask before each video:
.B y
(yes),
.B n
(no) or
.B a
(abort the whole run).
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-same\-dir
Save images next to the video file instead of in a new
.IR name _frames
folder.
.TP
.BR \-O ", " \-\-output " [\fIxx\fR]"
Write all images below the folder
.I xx
(default
.BR frames )
and keep the folder tree of the source, as
.IR xx /\fIsubfolder\fR/\fIname\fR_frames.
If
.I xx
already exists,
.IR xx _001,
.IR xx _002
and so on is used instead, so earlier output is never touched.
With
.BR \-D ,
the images of each source folder share one folder,
.IR xx /IsubfolderR,
instead of one folder per video.
If the last component of
.I xx
contains a dot (for example
.BR movie.mp4 ),
vfx asks for confirmation (y/n) before proceeding, since that is usually a
mistake.
If that folder name is already taken (a file counts), the question shows the
name that will be used instead, for example
.BR movie.mp4_001 .
Only
.B y
or
.B yes
proceeds; any other answer aborts.
Because the value is optional, put the source before
.BR \-O ,
or write
.BI \-\-output= xx\fR;
otherwise the source is taken as
.IR xx .
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-dry\-run
List the videos that would be processed and where the images would go,
without extracting anything.
Needs neither ffmpeg nor ffprobe.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version number and exit.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-h ", " \-? ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
One or more files failed, the source was not found, or ffmpeg is missing.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command line.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted.
.SH EXAMPLES
Sixteen evenly spaced frames from one file:
.PP
.RS
vfx movie.mp4
.RE
.PP
One frame every 10 seconds, in all subfolders:
.PP
.RS
vfx \-R \-T 10 ~/Videos
.RE
.PP
Every frame, as PNG:
.PP
.RS
vfx \-N 0 \-F png clip.mov
.RE
.PP
Show what would be processed:
.PP
.RS
vfx \-L \-R .
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR ffprobe (1)
